# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# The web build is a single-page app (app.json -> web.output: "single"), so
# only index.html is emitted and Expo Router resolves every route in the
# browser. Any deep link or refresh on a client-side route — /expenses,
# /account/<uuid>, /edit-expense/<uuid> — has no file of its own on disk and
# would 404 without this rule.
#
# Cloudflare Pages matches real static assets (the JS bundle, favicon,
# /assets/*) before applying _redirects, so this catch-all only fires for
# paths that aren't files. The 200 serves index.html in place rather than
# issuing a redirect, which keeps the requested URL in the address bar for
# the router to read.
/*    /index.html   200
